        "original_id": "e7994e55-c6e2-56b3-b5ae-ec3d89d9529f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Norris Dam State Park, Anderson County, Campbell County, Tennessee, Norris Lake, Clinch River, Tazewell, Virginia, Great Appalachian Valley, Kingston, Tennessee\n- Structures: Norris Dam\n\nFacts:\n- Norris Dam was completed in 1936.\n- Norris Lake is the impoundment of the Clinch River created by the completion of Norris Dam in 1936.\n- Norris Dam State Park is a 600 mile sized state park in Anderson County and Campbell County, Tennessee.\n- Norris Dam State Park is situated along the shores of Norris Lake.\n- The Clinch River rises near Tazewell, Virginia.\n- The Clinch River flows southwest for more than 300 miles through the Great Appalachian Valley.\n- The Clinch River joins the Tennessee River in Kingston, Tennessee.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1fd28f3c-c3d9-5688-b3aa-44e9b74f1bb6",
        "text": "Norris Dam State Park is a 600 mile sized state park in Anderson County and Campbell County, Tennessee, the park is situated along the shores of Norris Lake, and impoundment of the Clinch River created by the completion of Norris Dam in 1936, the Clinch River rises near Tazewell, Virginia, and flows southwest for more than 300 mi through the Great Appalachian Valley, at the end, it joins the Tennessee River in Kingston, Tennessee.",
