        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Norris Dam State Park, Norris Lake, Clinch River, Tazewell, Virginia, Great Appalachian Valley, Kingston, Tennessee\n- Structures: Norris Dam\n- Rivers: Powell River, Tennessee River\n\nFacts:\n- In 1936, Norris Dam was completed and created Norris Lake as an impoundment of the Clinch River.\n- Norris Dam State Park is situated along the shores of Norris Lake.\n- The Clinch River rises near Tazewell, Virginia.\n- The Clinch River flows southwest for more than 300 miles through the Great Appalachian Valley.\n- The Clinch River gathers tributaries including the Powell River.\n- The Clinch River joins the Tennessee River in Kingston, Tennessee.",
